{#-
  The description is free text and lands on a line ruff measures. Two bugs
  this shape avoids:

  1. Line length. A one-line docstring `"""name: description."""` overflowed
     ruff's 100-column limit on a 72-character description, so the generated
     project failed its own CI on the very first push, before a line of code
     existed. The summary line is now the name alone, and the description is
     wordwrapped well inside the limit set in pyproject.toml.
  2. A doubled period. The template appended `.` to a description that already
     ended in one, giving `...AMD mobo..`. `trim('.')` strips whatever is there
     so exactly one is emitted.
-#}
{% if description -%}
"""{{ project_name }}.

{{ description | trim | trim('.') | wordwrap(88) }}.
"""
{%- else -%}
"""{{ project_name }}."""
{%- endif %}

__version__ = "0.1.0"
